Z||000000||RossT||08-21-2000||12:40 PM||||Did fieros produced for California have anything different done to the emissions system? If someone in California wanted to buy an out of state 88gt, what would they have to have done to the emissions sysytem to have it comply (if anything) other than an emissions test?<BR>Someone in California is interested in one of my gt's, and is curious about the emissions.<P>Thanks.<P>Ross<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-21-2000||01:50 PM||||Ross,<P>The only real difference was with the EPROM.  I believe that a stock Fiero with a Federal chip (what all non-California Fieros came with) will pass their emissions tests.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||08-21-2000||02:41 PM||||Thanks Mike. (its the sunroof car not the t-top)!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||08-21-2000||03:06 PM||||Since it is an out of state car, it just needs to meet the Federal standards. I haven't compared the federal and California chips, but my bet is the difference are minor anyway. <P>As long as the emission equipment is working, there won't be any problems bring it into California. <P>Whatever you do, don't try to make it look like it is CA certified. You'll get busted for that in a second.||||reg||1
